    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_hicache_nixl_storage.py` fails intermittently in `base-b-test-1-gpu-small`. Example failing jobs: [#46780](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40713563072/job/122922742593) and `cc-fixes-rebased` (job 122948256119), both on 2026-10-28:\n\n```\nPOSIX path-mode open failed: nixl::FileFd(\"/tmp/test_nixl_unified/72/same_prefix_False_test_model_0_2_mamba\"): No such file or directory\nFAIL: test_mla_mamba_round_trip_keeps_each_tp_rank (zero_copy=False)\nAssertionError: Lists differ: [False] != [True]\n```\n\n**Cause:** `HiCacheNixl` starts `HiCacheL3Cleaner` on TP rank 0 by default (`l3_cleaner_enabled=True`, high watermark 80%). The cleaner thread runs its first tick immediately. If the filesystem holding the storage directory is at or above the watermark, it unlinks the oldest files. This test writes the rank-0 checkpoint first and then reads it back, so on a runner whose `/tmp` disk is near 80% full, the cleaner deletes that file before the read.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSet `\"l3_cleaner_enabled\": False` in the two file-backed configs that write from TP rank 0: `TestNixlUnified.setUp`, which the failing test inherits via `replace(...)`, and `_make_direct_io_hicache`. The cleaner keeps its own coverage in `test_hicache_nixl_cleaner.py`.\n\n## Checks\n\nThese were run on a B200 devbox (nixl 1.5.1) with this file run 10 times per row. To simulate a full disk, a wrapper lowers the cleaner's watermark to 0.1% and keeps the config's `enabled` flag:\n\n| | pass / fail |\n|---|---|\n| main, watermark forced low | 0 / 10, same missing-file error as CI |\n| this PR, watermark forced low | 10 / 0 |\n| this PR, default watermark | 10 / 0 |\n| `test_hicache_nixl_cleaner.py` | 10 / 0 |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40745490021](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40745490021)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40745487889](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40745487889)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40745487834](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40745487834)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
